wifi: ath11k: batch the TX completions of a poll

ath11k_dp_tx_completion_handler() takes the id table lock for each
completion, decrements the radio's pending MSDU count with a fully
ordered atomic for each, and touches the frame's buffer, control
buffer and shared info cold, one frame after the other.

Read up to 16 completions at a time, release the ids of all of them
under one hold of the lock, count the frames done in one atomic update
for each radio at the end of the poll, and prefetch the buffers of the
next two frames while the current one is completed. The pending count
drops after the frames' status has been reported instead of before it,
and before the starved mark is read, which is what the ordering of the
decrement is for. The completion of each frame is otherwise unchanged:
the status, the airtime refund of the frame and of the batch it belongs
to, the free list and the TXQ push run for each frame in the order of the
ring, so the AQL charge of a frame is refunded exactly once, and the
pending airtime of the stations and the radio returns to 0 at idle, as
the aql_audit debugfs files show. The statuses of the firmware's own
completions are handled in the same order as before.

The status parse starts from a cleared status for each completion, where
it used to reuse one that the flags of an earlier frame stayed in.

The ath11k.tx_compl_batch module parameter restores one lock hold and one
count update for each frame for an A/B.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -1430,6 +1430,39 @@ static inline void ath11k_dp_tx_status_p
 		ts->rate_stats = 0;
 }
 
+/* TEST-ONLY switch for the A/B of the completion run against one lock hold,
+ * one pending count update and a prefetch for each frame; dropped before this
+ * is upstreamed.
+ */
+static bool ath11k_tx_compl_batch = true;
+module_param_named(tx_compl_batch, ath11k_tx_compl_batch, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(tx_compl_batch,
+		 "Batch the TX completions of a poll (default: on)");
+
+#define ATH11K_DP_TX_COMPL_CHUNK 16
+
+struct ath11k_dp_tx_compl_item {
+	struct hal_tx_status ts;
+	struct ath11k_dp_tx_seg seg;
+	struct hal_wbm_release_ring *tx_status;
+	struct sk_buff *msdu;
+	u32 msdu_id;
+	u8 mac_id;
+	bool more;
+};
+
+/* A frame, or a segment of a batch, is done: counted at the end of the run,
+ * or at once when the batching is off.
+ */
+static void ath11k_dp_tx_done_one(struct ath11k *ar, u8 mac_id, bool batch,
+				  int *pending)
+{
+	if (batch)
+		pending[mac_id]++;
+	else if (atomic_dec_and_test(&ar->dp.num_tx_pending))
+		wake_up(&ar->dp.tx_empty_waitq);
+}
